# tally 2.3.1 S6, Q1.11, Q1.12 (L §5.11's aggregate paragraph: the tuple argmin, argmax, first or last returns
# compares with == and != key by key and stands in a key position of the same indexes): t1 false, t2, t3 true;
# v[argmin(…)] 3.00 PLN, v[first(…)] 5.00 PLN. S17: mean of rates keeps their unit (m1). Before: LOAD-UNIT
# `(key ks, key js) and (key ks, key js) compared` for the whole text.
=== tuple.tally
model tuple
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [k1, k2, k3]
index js = [j1, j2]
input v[k in ks, j in js]: money PLN
input r[k in ks]: rate
input best_k: key ks
input best_j: key js


ask t1: argmin(v[k, j] for k in ks, j in js) == argmax(v[k, j] for k in ks, j in js)
ask t2: argmin(v[k, j] for k in ks, j in js) != argmax(v[k, j] for k in ks, j in js)
ask t3: argmin(v[k, j] for k in ks, j in js) == argmin(v[k, j] for k in ks, j in js)
ask t4: v[argmin(v[k, j] for k in ks, j in js)]
ask t5: v[first(k in ks, j in js where v[k, j] > v[k2, j1])]
ask m1: mean(r[k] for k in ks)

version ver
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  v[k1, j1] = 5.00 PLN "s"
  v[k1, j2] = 7.00 PLN "s"
  v[k2, j1] = 3.00 PLN "s"
  v[k2, j2] = 9.00 PLN "s"
  v[k3, j1] = 4.00 PLN "s"
  v[k3, j2] = 6.00 PLN "s"
  r[k1] = 2 %/year "s"
  r[k2] = 4 %/year "s"
  r[k3] = 6 %/year "s"
  best_k = k2 "s"
  best_j = j1 "s"
=== expect
m1: 0.04 1/year
  cut 2026-10-18
t1: false
  cut 2026-10-18
t2: true
  cut 2026-10-18
t3: true
  cut 2026-10-18
t4: 3.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-18
t5: 5.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-18
